{
  "title": "Pangea™ Distal Posterior Tibia Plate",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423210/pangea-tm--distal-posterior-tibia-plate",
  "subtitle": "Tibial Shaft Fractures Updated: Jun 8 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea™ series contains 3 distal tibia plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Distal Anterolateral Tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Distal Medial Tibia**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Distal Posterior Tibia (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pangea Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive locking position in the plate’s locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V ELI material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423210/images/3e5743ad-2964-4d88-8e1a-be2523448cfe_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.38.27_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Circular universal holes accept nonlocking screws, and locking screws within a 30° cone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**1.6mm K-Wire Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "K-wire holes at distal aspect",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Oblong Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To aid in plate placement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**3.5mm Screws in the Shaft**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "3.5mm screw holes in the shaft and 2.7mm screw hole options distally for versatile fixation option",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423210/images/68f846a3-f087-41dd-b721-9c07c93e1c60_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.38.15_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2.7mm Distal Row**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Accepts variable angle locking screws to reduce the potential for implant prominence and allow for capture of articular fragments",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Distal Cluster**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to sit immediately medial to the posterior aspect of the tibial incisura",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423210/images/68f846a3-f087-41dd-b721-9c07c93e1c60_screenshot_2025-01-08_at_11.38.15_am.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The plate is placed on the posterior surface of the distal tibia, specifically to sit on the lateral side of the posterior surface over the posterior malleolus",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Proper position is achieved when the distal end of the plate is adjacent to the articular surface, allowing for the distal screws to support the plafond.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Contour of the distal plate is designed to allow placement immediately proximal to the joint line for rafting while reducing plate prominence.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Fit",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Distal Posterior Tibia Plate is designed to act as a buttress of the posterior malleolus or posterior fixation of pilon fractures.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The rotation of the plate is designed to allow for central placement on the tibial shaft while facilitating capture of the posterior malleolus.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The fit and placement is designed to reduce the potential for irritation of the flexor hallucis longus (FHL tendon).",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Designed with the use of SOMA: Stryker Orthopedics Modeling and Analytics.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "SOMA analysis shows better anatomic plate fit of the Distal Posterior Tibia plate compared to competitive VA-LCP distal tibia plates. 2",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea Tibia Plating System is indicated for the internal fixation and stabilization of tibia bone fractures and osteotomies in normal and osteopenic bone, including:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Diaphyseal, metaphyseal, epiphyseal, extra- and intra-articular fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Non-unions, malunions, and deformities",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Periprosthetic fractures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approaches",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Surgeons may use a posteromedial or posterolateral approach to the distal posterior tibia. When using a posterolateral approach, care must be taken to protect the sural nerve.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technical specifications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Standard plate lengths: 2-10 hole (75-187mm)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Shaft thickness: 3.3mm",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Distal thickness: 2.3mm",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Left and right anatomic plate options",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill bits for T8: Ø2.0mm x 135mm (542000(S)) Ø2.0mm x 175mm (542001(S))",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Drill bits for T15: Ø2.5mm x 135mm (542020) Ø2.5mm x 215mm (542021)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
